+  >
+  > **Pre-surgery preparation** Your surgeon will explain your procedure and individual recovery plan, and you may need to follow a specific pre-op diet to shrink your liver and reduce surgical risk (typically 2–4 weeks). But you won’t do it alone! Our staff will support you throughout.
+  >
+  > **Procedure day** Obesity Surgery WA’s bariatric surgery is performed via keyhole surgery in most cases, with short post-operative hospital stays (1-3 nights) at [Mount Private Hospital](https://mountprivatehospital.com.au), [The Park Private Hospital](https://www.tpph.com.au/), or [Waikiki Private Hospital](https://waikikiprivate.com.au/) in Perth. Guided by nursing and dietetic staff, you’ll start on fluids and your recovery will be monitored until you’re ready to return home.
+  >
+  > **Long-term aftercare** Most light daily activities can usually be resumed gradually from around the ~2-3 week mark, with return to work depending on which procedure you have and what type of work you do (~2+ weeks’ for desk work/4+ weeks for physical or manual labour). Your post-op progression from fluids only to regular textures will take place with the support of your dietitian. Plus you’ll need ongoing reviews (regularly post-op then annually) and bloodwork done to protect your nutrition and results long-term.
