+
+  > - [**Gastric sleeve (sleeve gastrectomy)**](/gastric-sleeve-perth): removes part of the stomach to create a smaller stomach. The surgeon will explain expected effects, risks, nutritional needs and whether it is appropriate for you; individual results vary.
+  > - [**Gastric bypass (Roux-en-Y)**](/gastric-bypass-perth): changes stomach size and how food passes through the small intestine. It has procedure-specific nutritional requirements and risks; your surgeon can explain why it may or may not be appropriate for your circumstances.
+  > - [**Mini gastric bypass (one anastomosis bypass)**](/mini-gastric-bypass): a bypass variation that creates a single connection between the stomach and small intestine. The surgeon can explain its technical features, risks, follow-up needs and whether it is appropriate for your circumstances.
+  > - [**Gastric band (adjustable band)**](/gastric-band): an implanted adjustable band that can be adjusted or removed, but still requires surgery, ongoing reviews and monitoring for band-related complications. Your surgeon can explain the expected follow-up and whether it is appropriate for you.
+  > - [**Revision surgery**](/revision-bariatric-surgery): may be discussed after a previous procedure when there are complications, a need for conversion or another clinical reason. Risks and follow-up differ by case and are assessed individually.
+  > - [**Medical weight management**](/non-surgical-weight-loss): a non-surgical pathway supported by medical assessment, dietitian input and long-term follow-up. Suitability should be assessed by the clinical team.
